@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
top to bottom direction
title Appointment Tracking System — conceptual domain model
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 55
hide methods
hide circle

' People and service catalogue
  class Patient {
    patientID
    firstName
    lastName
    dateOfBirth
    phone
    contactDetails
  }
  class PatientInsurance {
    kind: RAMQ / private
    insurerName
    insuranceNumber
    validityDetails [optional]
  }
  class HealthcareProfessional {
    professionalID
    name
    professionalInformation
    professionalKind: family physician /
      specialist physician / nurse / other
    practiceKind: clinic / external
  }
  class Specialty {
    specialtyID
    name
  }
  class ClinicLocation {
    locationID
    name
    address
    phone
    timeZone
  }
  class Service {
    serviceID
    name
    durationMinutes > 0
    requiresReferral
    coveragePolicy
    standardFee [optional]
  }

' Scheduling and encounters
  class Schedule {
    scheduleID
  }
  class AvailabilityPeriod {
    weekday
    localStartTime
    localEndTime
    effectiveFrom
    effectiveTo
  }
  class Appointment {
    appointmentID
    startTime
    bookedDurationMinutes
    status: requested / confirmed /
      completed / cancelled
    arrivalTime [optional]
  }
  class ClinicalRecord {
    clinicalRecordID
  }
  class Consultation {
    consultationID
    recordedAt
    observations [optional]
    diagnoses [optional]
    treatmentRecommendations [optional]
    followUpRequirements [optional]
  }

' Referral and prescribing
  class Referral {
    referralID
    issuedAt
    clinicalReason
    priority
    status
  }
  class Prescription {
    prescriptionID
    issuedAt
  }
  class PrescriptionItem {
    dosage
    instructions
  }
  class Medication {
    medicationID
    name
    strength [optional]
    form [optional]
  }

' Charges and recorded payments
  class Fee {
    feeID
    description
    amount
    currency
    coverageOutcome: uninsured
    coverageBasis
  }
  class Invoice {
    invoiceID
    issuedAt
    /total
    /outstandingBalance
    /status: unpaid / partiallyPaid / paid
  }
  class InvoiceLine {
    description
    quantity
    chargedUnitAmount
    currency
    /lineTotal
  }
  class Payment {
    paymentID
    paidAt
    amount
    currency
    method
    reference [optional]
  }

' Conceptual access and accountability
  class UserAccount {
    accountID
    accountStatus
  }
  class Role {
    roleName
    permissionScope
  }
  class AuditEvent {
    eventID
    occurredAt
    action
    targetType
    targetID [optional]
    outcome
    safeReasonCode [optional]
  }

Patient "1" -- "0..*" PatientInsurance : holds >
HealthcareProfessional "0..*" -- "0..*" Specialty : qualified in >
HealthcareProfessional "0..*" -- "0..*" ClinicLocation : practises at >
HealthcareProfessional "0..*" -- "0..*" Service : qualified to offer >
Service "0..*" -- "0..*" Specialty : qualification requirements >

HealthcareProfessional "1" -- "0..*" Schedule : has >
Schedule "1" *-- "0..*" AvailabilityPeriod : contains >
AvailabilityPeriod "0..*" --> "1" ClinicLocation : at
AvailabilityPeriod "0..*" -- "1..*" Service : permits >
Patient "1" -- "0..*" Appointment : attends >
HealthcareProfessional "1" -- "0..*" Appointment : treats >
ClinicLocation "1" -- "0..*" Appointment : hosts >
Service "1" -- "0..*" Appointment : booked for <
Patient "1" -- "1" ClinicalRecord : has >
ClinicalRecord "1" -- "0..*" Consultation : contains >
Appointment "1" -- "0..1" Consultation : documented by >
HealthcareProfessional "1" -- "0..*" Consultation : records >
Consultation "0..1" -- "0..*" Appointment : originates follow-ups >

Patient "1" -- "0..*" Referral : subject of >
HealthcareProfessional "1" -- "0..*" Referral : clinical author of >
Referral "0..*" --> "0..1" Specialty : target specialty
Referral "0..*" --> "0..1" HealthcareProfessional : target professional
Referral "0..1" -- "0..*" Appointment : supports >
Consultation "1" -- "0..*" Prescription : leads to >
HealthcareProfessional "1" -- "0..*" Prescription : prescribes >
Prescription "1" *-- "1..*" PrescriptionItem : contains >
PrescriptionItem "0..*" --> "1" Medication : identifies

Appointment "1" -- "0..*" Fee : assessed charges >
Patient "1" -- "0..*" Invoice : billed by >
Invoice "1" *-- "1..*" InvoiceLine : contains >
InvoiceLine "0..1" --> "1" Fee : bills once
Invoice "1" -- "0..*" Payment : settled by >

UserAccount "0..1" -- "0..1" Patient : own-patient identity >
UserAccount "0..1" -- "0..1" HealthcareProfessional : professional identity >
UserAccount "0..*" -- "1..*" Role : assigned >
UserAccount "1" -- "0..*" AuditEvent : accountable actor for >
AuditEvent "0..*" --> "0..1" Patient : affected patient

note top of ClinicLocation
  Clinic practitioners have >= 1 practice location.
  External referring professionals may have none,
  and need no clinic schedule or user account.
  Appointments/schedule periods use clinic practitioners
  at their assigned practice locations.
end note

note top of Service
  Service coveragePolicy: RAMQ-covered,
  uninsured, or conditional (working vocabulary).
  PatientInsurance is separate: being insured does
  not make every booked service covered.
  Duration and effective weekly availability are assumption A3.
  Appointment duration is captured when reserved;
  later catalogue edits cannot rewrite booked intervals.
end note

note bottom of Appointment
  Requested and confirmed appointments reserve
  [startTime, startTime + bookedDurationMinutes).
  Recheck schedule and patient/professional overlap
  across locations at request/reschedule time.
  Rescheduling changes time, never adds a status.
  Arrival is independent and requires confirmed
  status on the appointment location's local date.
  A successful follow-up is requested, reserves a
  slot, and has an originating consultation link.
end note

note bottom of Consultation
  Recording requires confirmed + arrived and
  the authorised treating professional.
  Create Consultation + ClinicalRecord association
  + completed Appointment + audit together.
  Appointment patient = ClinicalRecord patient;
  recording professional = appointment professional.
  At most one consultation per appointment (A7).
end note

note bottom of Referral
  {target specialty OR target professional OR both}
  At least one target must exist; both supplied
  targets constrain the selected service/professional.
  Appointment patient = referral patient.
  Required/supplied referrals must be usable.
  One referral may support many appointments.
  External authorship is retained when authorised
  clinic staff capture a referral (A8); the capturing
  account is in AuditEvent, not substituted as author.
  Status vocabulary/expiry remain open (A6).
end note

note bottom of PrescriptionItem
  Each issued prescription has >= 1 item.
  Every item requires medication, dosage,
  instructions; prescribing authority is checked.
  No electronic pharmacy delivery is modelled.
end note

note bottom of Invoice
  Invoice patient = each billed fee's appointment patient.
  An invoice can group charges from several appointments.
  Each fee is assessed against one appointment and billed
  at most once; lines preserve the charged amounts.
  Fee retains manually assessed uninsured outcome and
  administrative basis for this patient/service (O22).
  Covered/undetermined assessments cannot create fees;
  no electronic coverage adjudication is implied.
  /outstandingBalance = /total - recorded payments.
  Partial payments and one invoice per payment are A11.
  No claims submission or payment gateway.
end note

note bottom of Role
  Example roles: Patient; Administrative staff;
  Healthcare professional; Practice administrator;
  Audit reviewer (allocations A1/A10).
  Permissions also require own-patient / care scope;
  roles alone do not grant clinical access.
  Staff registration/arrival access does not imply
  access to clinical narratives or prescribing.
end note

note bottom of AuditEvent
  Audit successful writes, sensitive reads and denials.
  Keep actor, time, action, safe target IDs/outcome;
  no clinical content, medication details, raw search
  criteria, insurance numbers or request payloads.
  Optional target/patient IDs allow denied unknown IDs.
  Protect audit evidence; no ordinary-user rewriting (A12).
end note

legend bottom left
  Conceptual entities and facts only: no controllers, repositories or infrastructure classes.
  Association end multiplicities apply per instance at the opposite end.
  Shared aggregation is avoided; composition marks owned line/period/item parts.
  /attribute = derived value; [optional] = may be absent.
  Source: project-requirements pages 2–3; provisional analysis decisions D2–D7.
  A1–A12 label analyst assumptions explained in ../scenarios.md.
endlegend
@enduml
